# ── what is committed, and what is not ────────────────────────────────────
#
#   cohorts/    COMMITTED and persisting. The frozen splits, the cohort
#               assignment, and the clinical trait list. A run does not
#               regenerate these; deleting them loses the split.
#   genes/      COMMITTED. Curated gene sets, identical to the directory of the
#               same name in endotypes-transcriptomics.
#   ipynb/      COMMITTED, rendered, and holds notebooks and nothing else.
#   src/        COMMITTED. paths.R: locations only.
#   run_all.sh, README.md, endotypes-proteomics.yml   COMMITTED.
#
#   data/       NOT committed. The study download, and data/run_artifacts/,
#               which holds everything a run can regenerate.
#   figures/    COMMITTED. A 300 dpi PNG of every figure. A run regenerates them,
#               so they are reproducible rather than precious, but they are committed
#               so a figure can be taken into a slide or a manuscript without
#               re-running the pipeline.

data/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ipynb/ holds notebooks. Anything else that lands there is a stray -- the
# cohort CSVs live in cohorts/ and run output in data/run_artifacts/.
ipynb/artifacts/
ipynb/*.csv
ipynb/*.rds
ipynb/*.png
ipynb/*.svg
ipynb/*.pdf
ipynb/*.html
ipynb/.ipynb_checkpoints/

# R
permutedStats-*.RData          # WGCNA modulePreservation cache
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/

# macOS
.DS_Store
